From 0d4a03d6e3357cdf03e999c128281a638512d54d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rickow <30348240+Rickow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:11:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HSFA: "Stage-locked view" widescreen edges (default): the
 view slides to the stage ends, HUD stays centered

At the ends of a stage the arcade camera stops (scroll2 X = 0 / $180 on every
stage of the 5 games) and the stage art ends at the edge of the 4:3 view, so
the 64 px side bands of the 512 px picture had little real art there (21 to
32 % of the bands had to be invented by the mirror of patch 0022).

- New value of "Widescreen edges" (fbneo-hsfa-ws-edges): "stage"
  (Stage-locked view), now the default; mirror / repeat / black / raw kept.
  The game is unchanged (logic, camera, memory, sound). In fights the 4:3
  game view is no longer always centered: with m the shown band width,
  x = m in the middle of the camera course, x = camera near the left end
  (camera < m), x = camera - $180 + 2m near the right end, so the picture
  stays on the painted stage. x follows the camera, so it never jumps
  unless the camera does. Out of fights: centered, as before.
- Stage planes and scene sprites (characters, shadows, effects, stage
  sprites) are moved together: nCpsGlobalXOffset = x while drawing, sprites
  get the difference (nHsfaWsObjDx); their 10-bit X is read in [-256, 768)
  of the screen so that sprites of the right band beyond 512 do not wrap.
- The HUD stays centered (HsfaWsHud), measured on games of the 5 modules
  (screen-fixed while the camera moves) and checked with HUD-only /
  HUD-less renders: SFA3, system graphics (codes $16000-$19FFF); Upper,
  Upper MAX, Hyper, graft: sprites of list slot 1 (table plan2, system
  graphics), marked by HsfaEclater with bit 12 of the Y word (unused after
  the conversion; under HSFA_WS); all games: palette $1D, and palette $1E
  with codes $02xxx / $3Exxx / $3Fxxx (K.O., PERFECT, ROUND n banners).
  Life bars, timer, portraits, names, gauges (whole Hyper P2 gauge), GO!,
  combo texts, SUPER, isms stay in place.
- What is still missing (slow planes narrower than the picture, stale
  scroll1 columns, shorter rows): mirror of patch 0022, on bands of any
  width (0 to 2m). HSFA_WS_REPLI=black: black instead (tests).
- scroll1 (all modes but raw): a slow plane kept still in the 512 px ring
  also holds columns that the arcade never shows at any camera position
  (SFA3 $00: 461 px of sky and 51 px of other tiles, seen as an orange
  block at the left of the picture). In the bands a column is now shown
  only if the game rewrote it, if it was already seen in the 4:3 view, or
  if it lies in the range the view covers over the whole camera course
  (scroll1 X = a + k x camera, k measured once the camera moved 48 px,
  kept for the stage $FF8100; automatic scrolling: no restriction).
- Measured (camera forced to both ends and to the middle, all stages of SFA3
  and Upper, 4 Hyper, 5 Upper MAX, 3 graft): share of the bands without
  real art (ends and middle), centered 0022 -> stage-locked: SFA3 21 -> 5 %,
  Upper 21 -> 7 %, Upper MAX 32 -> 15 %, Hyper 32 -> 26 %, graft 32 -> 12 %.
- Checks: 4:3 core unchanged (all under HSFA_WS); 14:9 + raw = former
  448 px core to the pixel; mirror / black / repeat: 4:3 view unchanged
  (bands: scroll1 filter); stage-locked view without the HUD: 4:3 view
  identical to the 4:3 core, only moved (252 captures, all stages); logs
  and sound identical; Skip idle loops On and Off. Cost: same as mirror
  within the noise of the test machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
